id: decisions/037-every-record-names-its-shape-source
title: "Every record names where its shape came from"
kind: decision-frame
record_shape: header
status: draft
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Claude Code session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-12; drafted from the JUDGMENTS.md reversal axis 'provenance-retention'; recommendation is an attributed inference and ratifies nothing"
version: "1.0.0"
updated: 2026-09-12
template_ref: templates/decision.yawn
principal_ref: principal:dave

axis: provenance-retention
axis_gloss: "whether the original wording, shape and cost of an input survive into the record, or only a cleaned, normalised form does"
poles:
  a: raw-source-preserved
  b: normalised-only
split: lone-exception
draft_status: full
leverage: 7.2
leverage_formula: "judgments_resolved(15) x split_weight(0.4) x authored_conflict_bonus(1.2)"

question: >
  Must every record say which template it was copied from, or is a spec or
  schema version enough for the newer families that carry one?

why_it_matters: >
  The repo keeps raw wording, raw email bodies and the owner's exact words
  beside every interpretation, and never lets a rendering stand in for what
  arrived; the one place it drops lineage is the record's own shape, where the
  1.0 human family carries source.template and every newer family carries a
  version tag instead. Once answered, a bot that reads a record knows what to
  diff it against — the template file or the schema — and a child Yawn copying a
  template knows which back-pointer it must keep.

state_snapshot:
  description: >
    14 judgments sit at raw-source-preserved (7 authored) and 1 at normalised-only
    (0 authored). The repository asserts both directions on this axis.
  attributed_to: JUDGMENTS.md
  epistemic_status: observed
  source_refs:
    - JUDGMENTS.md
    - TAXONOMY.md

lacuna:
  kind: unselected_choice
  description: >
    Whether Dave regards a schema version as lineage at all, or only as a
    validation target.

options:
  - name: A
    description: >
      rule: Every record, in every family, carries a back-pointer to the template it
      was copied from (source.template for YAML records, sourceTemplate for the two
      JSON contracts). A version tag identifies a contract, not the file the record
      was made from, so it does not replace the pointer.
    cost: "One line in roughly twenty templates; the two JSON templates gain a key their schemas must allow."
    risk: "Redundant with spec_version on the q-space and contract families; two identity fields drift apart."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "Extend tests/record-shape.test.mjs (in-flight): every template carries source.template (or sourceTemplate) equal to its own path, so copies inherit it; today twelve of thirty-two pass."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0156"
      - "J0200"
      - "J0346"
      - "J0431"
      - "J0511"
      - "J0643"
  - name: B
    description: >
      rule: A version identifier is sufficient lineage. source.template is dropped
      from the 1.0 family; a record is identified by spec_version, schemaVersion or
      record_shape alone.
    cost: "Twelve templates lose a field; the newcomer who copied templates/basic.yawn can no longer be told which file to diff against."
    risk: "Two records of the same spec_version made from different templates are indistinguishable, which is the one thing the raw-source rule elsewhere refuses to allow."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "None needed to drop a field; the record would be removing source.template from the twelve templates and the sentence in templates/node.yawn saying why."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0840"
  - name: C
    description: >
      rule: Every record names the artifact its shape came from, and
      templates/node.yawn record_shapes.rule says which field each shape uses:
      header-shape records carry source.template; spec-version and coordinate shapes
      carry spec_version and kind; json-contract shapes carry schemaVersion. A
      record missing its shape's identity field is malformed.
    cost: "One paragraph in templates/node.yawn; the in-flight record_shape registry already lists every template's shape."
    risk: "Three lineage conventions remain three; a reader still has to know which one to look for."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "Extend tests/record-shape.test.mjs: for each registered shape, assert the template carries that shape's identity field (source.template for header, spec_version for spec-version and coordinate, schemaVersion for json-contract)."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0346"
      - "J0643"
      - "J0840"

recommendation:
  option_ref: C
  confidence: 0.6
  epistemic_status: inferred
  authority: none
  reasoning: >
    The seven authored judgments are about preserving raw inputs, not about
    template back-pointers, so they do not settle this directly; the single
    exception is a revealed pattern across three template families and the
    in-flight record_shape registry has already committed to those families
    coexisting. Given that, saying which identity field each family owns (C) is
    cheaper and more honest than forcing one field onto grammars that already have
    an equivalent (A). A is the simplest uniform rule and is close; it wins if
    Dave wants one back-pointer a newcomer can always find.

target_condition:
  mode: decide
  proposed_by: agent-on-behalf
  affected_principals:
    - principal:dave
  ratification_status: proposed
  sufficient_when:
    - "templates/node.yawn record_shapes.rule names the identity field for each shape."
    - "Every template carries the identity field its registered shape requires, and a test in tests/ rejects one that does not."
    - "No template carries both a source.template and a spec_version that disagree about its family."

choice:
  selected_by: ""
  option_ref: ""
  authority_ref: ""

proof:
  covers:
    - target_condition
    - options
  falsifier: >
    A new template lands with neither source.template nor a version field and the
    record-shape test passes.
  status: proposed

resolves:
  - "J0156"
  - "J0200"
  - "J0346"
  - "J0431"
  - "J0511"
  - "J0643"
  - "J0840"

boundary:
  - "confidence cannot ratify an objective; this record proposes and Dave decides"
  - "the REVEALED judgments cited here describe what artifacts do, not what Dave chose"

source:
  template: templates/decision.yawn
  axis: TAXONOMY.md
  inventory: JUDGMENTS.md
